#: manifest.json
msgid "Some videos are larger than their picture: a 2560×1440 picture in a corner of a 3840×2160 video, the rest one solid colour. Auto Frame finds the picture when a video file on this computer starts and crops the video to it, so the picture fills the window. It reads a few frames of the file with the player's FFmpeg, remembers the answer per file and says on the video what it did. Video ▸ Auto Frame turns it on and off, detects again, and shows the full picture of one file."
